<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>If you are comparing detached garage builders in Calgary, start with the scope, not the sticker price. A typical back-lane garage is a slab, a framed box, a roof, siding to match the house, an overhead door, a man door and an electrical sub-panel, and two quotes that both say 'double garage' can leave different items out. Back Lane Garage Co is an advertising site that puts Calgary homeowners in touch with independent garage builders. It does not build, pull permits or hold a licence, and the builder who quotes your job contracts with you directly.</p><p>This page covers what a build includes, how single, double and triple garages differ, the steps the City of Calgary sets, and what to get in writing before you sign. Every price is named to the firm that advertises it, and every permit figure comes from the City. The City's own pages say they are not an official interpretation of the bylaws, so confirm your lot with the City before you commit. For the wider picture see the <a href='/'>homepage</a> and <a href='/garage-building-cost-calgary/'>garage building cost in Calgary</a>.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Slab and foundation scope</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Advertised packages list a 4-inch slab with a curb or thickened edge. The City says a slab over 55 m² (592 sq ft) without a foundation 1.2 m below grade needs a slab designed by a professional engineer.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Frame, roof and siding to match</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Published packages list 2 x 4 stud framing and vinyl siding to match the main dwelling. Ask each builder to write down wall height, roof type and siding in the quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Overhead door and man door</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Advertised door sizes include 16x7 and 16' x 8', with taller 18' wide options listed as add-ons by one builder. Door size drives what fits inside, so settle it before the drawings.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Electrical by a Master Electrician</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The City says every new garage needs a separate electrical permit for lights and the overhead door connection. When an electrical contractor does the work, only a Master Electrician can obtain that permit.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Single, double or triple</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Advertised starting prices run from $18,500 + GST (Corsac Construction, single 12' x 20') to $49,000 + GST (Corsac, triple 36' x 20'). Inclusions differ by firm, so compare scope line by line.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">City permit and inspections</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The City lists a 2026 new-garage building permit at $333.84 with a review of approximately 7 days. A framing inspection at lock-up stage is usually the main inspection.</p>
      </div>
</div>
